    size: { weightKg: [468, 490], typicalKg: 486, withersCm: null, girthCm: null, cannonCm: null, build: 'tall', notes: 'netkeiba 馬体重 over 13 starts: 474 at debut, 490 in the 1995 Asahi Hai, 486 in the 1996 Tenno Sho, 468 in the 1997 Takarazuka Kinen. No measurements published. Photos show a tall, long-legged, long-bodied horse with a long neck and refined head; the farm called him 「アカ抜けていた」 (ja.wikipedia). Nothing marks him as unusual, so no conf.' },
    gear: { hood: false, hoodColors: null, blinkers: false, shadowRoll: false, bitLifter: false, bridle: '#1c1a19', pompom: null, bandages: null, notes: 'Black bridle with a ring bit. No hood, blinkers or bandages in any photo. Wore a thick royal-blue (#2a4fb8) sheepskin shadow roll as a 2-3yo: 1995 Asahi Hai 3歳S finish (netkeiba photos 1238/1240) and 1996 Spring S paddock (1239). It is not visible in the 1996 Tenno Sho finish photo (JRA-VAN) or in the 1997 Takarazuka, Mainichi Okan, Tenno Sho and Japan Cup paddock photos.' },
    silks: { owner: '社台レースホース (Shadai Race Horse)', desc: 'Yellow with black vertical stripes; yellow sleeves with one blue hoop (黄、黒縦縞、袖青一本輪)', colors: ['#f2d000', '#111111', '#1f4fa8'] },
    saddleNumber: 4, // 1996 Tenno Sho (Autumn): 2枠4番 (JRA result archive; also netkeiba)
    career: 'Asahi Hai Sansai Stakes (G1, 1995); Spring Stakes (G2, 1996); Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1, 1996), the first post-war 3yo winner and the first since Happy Might in 1937; Naruo Kinen and Mainichi Okan (G2, 1997); 2nd in the 1997 Takarazuka Kinen and Tenno Sho (Autumn), 3rd in the 1997 Japan Cup. 13 starts, 7 wins.',
