    gear: { hood: true, hoodColors: { main: '#22a99a', trim: '#22a99a', ears: '#22a99a' }, blinkers: false, shadowRoll: '#1f9a6a', bitLifter: false, bridle: '#f2f0ea', pompom: null, bandages: null, notes: '2000 Takamatsunomiya Kinen (JRA-VAN and JRA photos): a teal or emerald-green menko with white polka dots on the crown and ear covers, matching the owner silks, plus a green sheepskin shadow roll. At his 1997 debut (Commons photo) he had no hood, a white shadow roll and a white noseband and bridle. The small 2000 winner-circle photo shows white on one hind lower leg that could not be settled as a marking or a bandage. The debut photo shows dark hind pasterns.' },
