    coat: { reg: '芦毛', key: 'ashige', greyness: 0.6, tone: 0, mane: '#6a6866', tail: '#d6d3cd', notes: 'Registered 芦毛 (JBIS, ja.wikipedia, netkeiba). His dam ポイントフラッグ and damsire メジロマックイーン were both 芦毛. He whitened steadily while racing (photos): a darker iron grey in 2012, a dappled mid-dark grey in 2013, and in the 2014 Takarazuka Kinen (the signature race) a paler dappled grey, light over the back and barrel with darker dapple rings and flecks on the neck and shoulder, dark grey lower legs, a grey mane with darker strands and a silvery-white tail. greyness is set for 2014 (about 0.35 in 2012, about 0.7 by 2015).' },
    face: { type: 'snip', notes: 'photo only: in the 2012 Arima Kinen winner photo (face-on) there is a patch of pink skin on the muzzle between the nostrils, running onto the lower nasal bone; pink skin on a grey shows white hair underneath, so this is a snip. The rest of his face had already gone nearly white, so a star or stripe above it cannot be seen either way. No text source names a marking.' },
    legs: { LF: 'none', RF: 'none', LH: 'coronet', RH: 'sock' }, // photo: RH white from the coronet to about mid-cannon over a pale hoof (2012 Kikuka off side, 2014 Hanshin Daishoten near side); LH a thin white coronet band over a striped hoof (2013 and 2014 Takarazuka); the fores dark grey to dark hooves
    style: { primary: 'oikomi', secondary: 'senko', why: 'netkeiba 通過, first call / field: Sapporo 2yo S 13/13, Radio NIKKEI Hai 14/16, Satsuki 18/18 (18-18-17-6, the win), Derby 13/18, Kobe Shimbun Hai 12/15, Kikuka 17/18 (17-17-4-2, the win), Arima 2012 16/16 (16-15-14-10, the win), Tenno Sho (Spring) 2013 14/18, JC 2013 16/17, Arima 2013 12/16, Tenno Sho (Spring) 2014 18/18, Arima 2014 11/16, Tenno Sho (Spring) 2015 14/17 (14-14-3-4, the win), Takarazuka 2015 16/16. Further forward in the Kyodo Tsushin Hai 4/11, Kyoto Daishoten 3/13, Hanshin Daishoten 2014 2/9, and both Takarazuka wins, 2013 4/11 and 2014 4/12. ja.wiki 特徴: 「ダッシュが利かない…先行策が難しく後方からのレースが多かった」; Iuzaki: 「3コーナーからロングスパート」. A long-run makuri closer from the back.' },
    size: { weightKg: [496, 516], typicalKg: 504, withersCm: null, girthCm: null, cannonCm: null, build: 'heavy', notes: 'db.netkeiba race-day 馬体重: 502 at his debut, lightest 496 (2011 Cosmos Sho), heaviest 516 (2015 AJCC, +6). Weights in his G1 wins: Satsuki 498, Kikuka 500, Arima 2012 506, Takarazuka 2013 500, Takarazuka 2014 504 (-2), Tenno Sho (Spring) 2015 510. ja.wiki: his dam was a 500 kg+ 大型馬, and he 「想定に反して大きく産まれた」; 身体面: 「後肢の繋ぎが顕著に緩く」, slow to accelerate, with 「大きなストライド」. No measurements were found.' },
    gear: { hood: true, hoodColors: { main: '#1c1e24', trim: '#1c1e24', ears: '#1c1e24' }, blinkers: true, blinkerColor: '#1c1e24', shadowRoll: '#1a1a1a', bitLifter: false, bridle: '#1a1a1a', pompom: null, bandages: null, tailRibbon: '#d22630', notes: 'His 2014 to mid-2015 look, matching the signature race. ja.wiki: blinkers first at the 2013 Arima Kinen, and at the 2014 Takarazuka 「ブリンカーに加えシャドーロールも着用」; both came off for the 2015 JC (「2013年の有馬記念以来となる…素顔」). Photos (2014 Takarazuka race and paddock, 2014 Arc paddock, 2015 Tenno Sho race): a near-black blinker hood with black ear covers, pale grey-lined blinker cups and "Gold Ship" in gold script on the side, and a thick black sheepskin shadow roll. Before Dec 2013 he raced bare-faced (the Satsuki, Kikuka, Arima 2012 and Takarazuka 2013 wins). Unbandaged legs. A red ribbon (kicker warning) is tied in the top of his tail in the 2013-2014 photos.' },
    silks: { owner: '小林英一 (JBIS: 合同会社小林英一ホールディングス)', desc: '赤、白袖赤一本輪', colors: ['#d8301e', '#ffffff'] },
    saddleNumber: 11, // 2014 宝塚記念 (Hanshin, 29 Jun 2014): 8枠11番 of 12 under 横山典弘, won by 3 lengths, the first horse to win the race twice (db.netkeiba, ja.wiki table; "11 ゴールドシップ" on the saddle cloth in both Commons 20140629 photos). Other G1 wins: Satsuki 2012 = 14, Kikuka 2012 = 1, Arima 2012 = 13, Takarazuka 2013 = 10, Tenno Sho (Spring) 2015 = 1
